  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 200 AM EDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThe extended period becomes a little tricky, not because of the\nsynoptic upper level pattern, but due to the timing of a wave of\ntropical moisture between pockets of SAL. In general though,\nglobal ensembles are within about 12 hours or so of each other \nwith the arrival of the brief period of enhanced tropical \nmoisture. What this ends up looking like is a day of more isolated\nstorm coverage on Friday with at least some SAL influence, \nincreased rain chances on Saturday, and then a prolonged period of\ndrier conditions Sunday into next week.\n\nRegardless of rain chances, the deep layer ridging mentioned above\nwill become re-established and anomalously strong for this time of\nyear. Highs in the middle to upper 90s, with heat indices well\ninto Advisory levels are expected for much of the period.",
